iversity of Graz is a university in Main building of the University of Graz, established in 1585. Holds notable historical significance, documented across 53 language editions of Wikipedia. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The University of Graz, founded in 1585 in Graz, Austria, stands as one of the oldest universities in the German-speaking world, playing a pivotal role in the intellectual landscape of Early Modern Europe. It emerged during a transformative period marked by the Reformation and the Counter-Reformation, attracting significant figures such as philosopher and theologian Franz von Ketteler and later becoming a hub for Enlightenment thought. Its establishment marked a key moment in the institutionalization of higher education, setting the stage for the university model that would proliferate across Europe.

